---
import Chapter from '../Chapter.astro';
import Print from '../Print.astro';
import ToolTag from '../ToolTag.astro';
import RadioFilm from '../../graphics/RadioFilm.astro';
import radio from '../../assets/photos/radio-air.jpg';
import film from '../../assets/photos/film-dd-bbc.jpg';
---
<Chapter id="ch-03" num="03" end="ask the question nobody asks.">
  <RadioFilm slot="graphic" />
  <Fragment slot="prints">
    <Print src={radio} alt="Close-up of the All India Radio studio desk: rows of switches, knobs and small red lights." caption="All India Radio. Filming wasn't allowed, so here's the desk." tilt={-2} />
    <Print src={film} alt="Anmol operating a camera on a shoulder rig, lit in deep red, on a film shoot." caption="On a short film with Doordarshan and BBC India." tilt={3} />
  </Fragment>
  <p class="beat">Then came the respectable degree, because middle-class Indian parents. Journalism and mass communication at Amity.</p>
  <p class="beat">Radio first. A summer at All India Radio turned into on-call work, and taught me that a listener can't see you, so every word has to earn its place.</p>
  <p class="beat">Then film. I learned Premiere from YouTube and directed a public service short that won first prize at college. Then newsrooms, at Doordarshan and BBC India.</p>
  <p class="beat">Journalism taught me the thing design school later confirmed. Don't start with what you want to say. Start with what you need to understand.</p>
  <ToolTag tool="Premiere Pro" />
  <blockquote slot="after" class="pull"><p>The brief is evidence. It isn't always the problem.</p></blockquote>
</Chapter>
